      "source_excerpt": "FDA Clinical Review §7.3.1 Deaths and Statistical Review Table 13, Summary of Adverse Events (SES): \"There were no deaths reported in the NAFT-500 Cream, 2% clinical development program.\" \"One SAE of influenza was reported in the tinea pedis study in a subject assigned to the Naftin® 1% Cream\" \"Summary of Adverse Events (SES)\" \"Tinea Pedis Trial\" \"Table 13.\" \"Summary of Adverse Events (SES)\" \"NAFT-500 Vehicle (2wk) Naftin 1% Vehicle (4wk)\" \"N=234 N=118 N=236 N=119\" -- FDA section 7.3.1 states that there were no deaths in the NAFT-500 Cream 2% clinical development program. The statistical review's Tinea Pedis Trial safety table gives the SES denominators for the four NCT arms. The clinical review's explicit tinea pedis SAE narrative supports that this trial is included in the program; all four arm counts are therefore zero. Percentages were not printed in this evidence and remain null. Each n_affected=0 is the literal-count representation of the source’s explicit statement that no deaths were reported; zero is not inferred from silence.",
